<article class="project"><a href="/work" class="project__back project__back--top">← Work</a><header class="project__hero"><div class="project__hero-media project__hero-media--shot"><a class="pshot pshot--link" href="https://github.com/Nizamohammed/Scribepad" target="_blank" rel="noopener" aria-label="View the ScribePad code on GitHub"><img src="/project/scribepad.jpg" alt="ScribePad"><span class="pshot__cue">View on GitHub</span></a></div><div class="project__hero-heading"><h1 class="project__title page-heading-reveal">ScribePad</h1><p class="project__hero-sub">A transcription tool for the command line.</p><div class="project__hero-actions"><a class="project__hero-cta" href="https://github.com/Nizamohammed/Scribepad" target="_blank" rel="noopener">View on GitHub</a></div></div></header><div class="project__meta"><span class="project__status"><span class="project__status-dot project__status-dot--done" aria-hidden="true"></span>Completed</span><span aria-hidden="true">·</span><span>Nov 2025 to Dec 2025</span><span aria-hidden="true">·</span><span>Personal project</span></div><section class="project__section"><p class="project__label">About</p><div class="project__body"><p>ScribePad is a Python command-line tool I built to turn long-form audio into clean, structured notes. It runs local speech-to-text models to produce timestamped transcripts, then a tuned language-model layer reshapes the output into lecture-style outlines with headings and key ideas.</p></div></section><section class="project__section"><p class="project__label">Highlights</p><div class="project__body"><ul class="project__list"><li>Generates timestamped transcripts from long-form audio using local speech-to-text models, with cleaned Markdown export.</li><li>Prototyped a notes layer that converts transcripts into lecture-style outlines with headings, key ideas, and worked examples.</li><li>Built around tuned language-model prompts for the structuring step.</li></ul></div></section><section class="project__section"><p class="project__label">Stack</p><div class="project__body"><ul class="project__chips"><li class="project__chip">Python</li><li class="project__chip">Markdown</li><li class="project__chip">CLI</li><li class="project__chip">local STT</li></ul></div></section><a href="/work" class="project__back project__back--bottom">← Work</a></article>
